WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.040
A return to an apocalyptic demolition&nbsp;
derby wasteland. Another adventure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.560
inside a deadly, neon video game. And&nbsp;
the revisitation of a Halloween classic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:16.000
All this and more await you with these&nbsp;
movie sequels you may not have heard about.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.280
The first Predator film tore into theaters&nbsp;
in 1987, launching a whole franchise that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:27.600
has endured across decades. And now, almost&nbsp;
inevitably, a fifth film is on the horizon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.560
The most recent installment, 2018's The Predator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.680
was hardly a critical success, currently&nbsp;
sitting at a dismal 33% on Rotten Tomatoes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.200
but it still made enough money at the&nbsp;
box office to justify yet another sequel.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.680
"Never knew how much I missed this,&nbsp;
Dutch." "You never were that smart."

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.960
Predator 5 will be helmed by 10 Cloverfield&nbsp;
Lane director Dan Trachtenberg , from a script&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:55.600
penned by budding screenwriter Patrick Aison.&nbsp;
Originally, the fifth Predator film was announced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.480
under the title Skulls, but the official&nbsp;
title has since been confirmed as Prey.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.440
Each Predator installment thus far has focused&nbsp;
on a group of people being hunted by a race of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.480
alien trophy hunters, and Prey seems like&nbsp;
it will follow in that same tradition.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:16.400
This time, the story will be set 300 years in&nbsp;
the past and center on the Comanche Nation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.040
following a warrior named Naru, who&nbsp;
will be played by Amber Midthunder.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.480
While the fifth Predator seemed to&nbsp;
hit an unforeseen snag in the form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.160
of a lawsuit filed by the original&nbsp;
film's writers Jim and John Thomas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:31.520
that apparently didn't stop the&nbsp;
movie from moving forward. Prey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:37.360
wrapped filming in September 2021, and is set&nbsp;
to premiere on Hulu sometime in summer 2022.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.280
While Hocus Pocus failed to make much of a&nbsp;
splash when it was first released in 1993,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.760
it has since gathered a significant&nbsp;
following as a Halloween staple. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:52.720
film follows a group of kids who accidentally&nbsp;
resurrect a trio of witches on Halloween,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:57.840
three hundred years after their execution.&nbsp;
The sisters set about stealing the souls of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.080
every child in Salem, unless these&nbsp;
intrepid heroes can stop them.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.200
While details on the sequel film remain scarce,&nbsp;
original Hocus Pocus stars Bette Midler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.000
Kathy Najimy, and Sarah Jessica Parker are set&nbsp;
to return in the sequel, which will debut on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:18.160
Disney+ in the fall of 2022. Some of the movie's&nbsp;
most notable cast members include Doug Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:23.600
reprising his role from the original, as well as&nbsp;
Tony Hale, Hannah Waddingham, and Sam Richardson.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.480
Working from a script by Jen D'Angelo, Hocus&nbsp;
Pocus 2 was originally set to be directed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.280
Adam Shankman, but he was replaced in&nbsp;
2021 by comedy stalwart Anne Fletcher.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.240
According to an official synopsis for the&nbsp;
film, Hocus Pocus 2 will follow three young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.320
women as they bring the Sanderson&nbsp;
sisters back to modern day Salem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:46.080
forcing them to stop the three witches&nbsp;
from wreaking havoc in the modern world.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.120
Before John Boyega was known for&nbsp;
battling the First Order in Star Wars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.840
he was fighting unsettling monstrous&nbsp;
aliens in the urban sci-fi adventure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:01.440
Attack the Block. Written and directed by Joe&nbsp;
Cornish, the 2011 film starred Boyega as Moses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:06.400
the leader of a teenage street gang that must rid&nbsp;
their neighborhood of invading extraterrestrials.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:11.440
The sequel will reunite Boyega and Cornish,&nbsp;
who's once again both writing and directing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:14.400
This time, Boyega will also&nbsp;
be acting as co-producer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.800
in addition to reprising his role as&nbsp;
Moses. Speaking to Deadline, Boyega said:

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:24.320
"It's been a decade since Attack the Block was&nbsp;
released, and so much has changed since then.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.760
I'm excited to see this heightened&nbsp;
story return to the streets of London.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:34.000
Moses has remained one of my favorite characters&nbsp;
to play and bringing him back is a huge honor."

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.480
Cornish echoed his enthusiasm, saying:

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.560
"I'm thrilled we're officially announcing&nbsp;
our return to the world of Attack the Block&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:46.160
on the tenth anniversary of the film's release.&nbsp;
I can't wait to work alongside John again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.880
bringing audiences an even bigger&nbsp;
slice of inner-city alien action."

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:56.080
According to Cornish, filming on Attack the Block&nbsp;
2 is expected to start at some point in 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.840
indicating that the movie might&nbsp;
premiere as early as 2023.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.360
Within days of the simultaneous&nbsp;
theatrical and HBO Max release of Dune,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:10.160
a sequel was officially greenlit, with&nbsp;
a release date set for October 20th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:16.240
2023. The decision to produce Dune: Part Two won't&nbsp;
come as a shock to anyone who knows the novel or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:21.200
saw the first film, which ended at what seemed to&nbsp;
be a pretty pivotal moment in the character arc of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:27.440
protagonist Paul Atreides. Dune began a sprawling&nbsp;
tale of feuding households, political maneuvering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:32.960
and religious intrigue, told through an&nbsp;
impressive ensemble cast led by Timothée Chalamet.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.760
Of course, not all the central players in&nbsp;
Dune survived until the end, but those that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.240
did are expected to reprise their roles in&nbsp;
the sequel. It's also a given that Zendaya,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.840
whose character is only introduced&nbsp;
towards the tail-end of the original,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.400
will be playing a much bigger role in this&nbsp;
installment. Also returning are director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:55.760
Denis Villeneuve and composer Hans Zimmer,&nbsp;
the latter of whom recently joked in a tweet:

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:58.720
"Thank goodness I have some music left."

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.880
As for Villeneuve, the director clarified&nbsp;
that he considers Dune: Part Two the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:07.280
movie as Dune rather than a traditional&nbsp;
sequel, telling The Hollywood Reporter:

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.880
"It's not a sequel where it's another&nbsp;
episode or another story with the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.720
characters. It actually has direct&nbsp;
continuity to the first movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:19.120
It's the second part of the big,&nbsp;
huge movie that I'm trying to do."

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.360
Unlike the original, Part Two&nbsp;
will not debut on HBO Max,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:28.160
instead receiving an exclusive&nbsp;
45-day theatrical window. Apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.320
this was a "non-negotiable" point for&nbsp;
Villeneuve, who says that for him:

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:37.760
"The theatrical experience is at the&nbsp;
very heart of the cinematic language."

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:40.080
"Oh, what a day! What a lovely day!"

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:48.320
In 2015, Mad Max: Fury Road reinvigorated the&nbsp;
long-dormant Mad Max franchise, which began in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:54.480
1979 with Mel Gibson in the title role. Fury Road&nbsp;
offered a new spin on the post-apocalyptic tale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.480 --> 00:06:00.560
casting Tom Hardy as Max and shifting focus to&nbsp;
Charlize Theron's rage-fueled Imperator Furiosa.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:05.200
Fury Road also wowed audiences and&nbsp;
critics alike, with many considering it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:11.200
one of the best action films of all&nbsp;
time. A sequel, then, seemed inevitable.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:16.160
Sure enough, two follow-up films are in the&nbsp;
works: one is a direct sequel, while the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:20.880
is a prequel centered around a younger Furiosa.&nbsp;
The sequel, which has been given the working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:26.480
title Mad Max: The Wasteland, was reportedly&nbsp;
greenlit by Warner Bros. in early 2020, and will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:32.000
follow Hardy's Max Rockatansky. Meanwhile, Furiosa&nbsp;
will bring back the title character in question,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:36.560
though Theron won't be making an appearance in&nbsp;
the movie. Director George Miller has said that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:40.400
much as he loved Theron's performance in&nbsp;
Fury Road, he doesn't have enough faith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:44.640
in de-aging technology to allow Theron&nbsp;
to reprise her role for the prequel.

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:48.160
Instead, the younger Furiosa will&nbsp;
be played by Anya Taylor-Joy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:54.320
who will be joined by MCU star Chris Hemsworth.&nbsp;
Emmy-winning Watchmen actor Yahya Abdul-Mateen II&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:59.040
was also set to star in the sequel but later&nbsp;
departed the project due to scheduling conflicts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.880
Instead, Tom Burke will be stepping into the&nbsp;
role originally intended for Abdul-Mateen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:08.400
Miller hasn't yet revealed who Hemsworth and Burke&nbsp;
will be playing in Furiosa, but the characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.680
have likely existed in the director's head since&nbsp;
before the previous film, as he and co-writer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:19.440
Nick Lathouris developed origin stories for every&nbsp;
character while prepping Fury Road. The Wasteland&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:26.160
is set for release on June 23rd, 2023, while&nbsp;
Furiosa will tear into theaters on May 27th, 2024.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:33.440
The Star Trek franchise has been a shining gem&nbsp;
in Paramount's crown for decades, and there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.640
a number of directions the popular franchise could&nbsp;
head next. Moving forward right now is a fourth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:43.840
Star Trek film in the current series, which would&nbsp;
bring back the cast of 2009's Star Trek and its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:49.920
sequels — minus Anton Yelchin, who was tragically&nbsp;
killed in an accident in 2016. The studio is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.720
considering Trek films from The Revenant scribe&nbsp;
Mark L. Smith, which was originally intended to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.720 --> 00:08:00.320
be directed by Quentin Tarantino, as well as&nbsp;
one from Fargo and Legion creator Noah Hawley.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:05.280
While Hawley's project has been moved to the back&nbsp;
burner by Paramount, Star Trek 4 is reportedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:09.600
full steam ahead. WandaVision director Matt&nbsp;
Shakman has signed on to helm the project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:14.800
working off a script from Lindsey Beer and Geneva&nbsp;
Robertson-Dworet — making this the first Star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:20.880
Trek film to be penned by women. Star Trek 4&nbsp;
is set to hit theaters on December 22, 2023.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:27.120
Although rumor has it that a third Sherlock Holmes&nbsp;
film has always been part of the Warner Bros.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:32.400
plan, things have been a little slow recently,&nbsp;
since Robert Downey Jr. has spent the past decade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:37.040
anchoring the Marvel Cinematic Universe. Saving&nbsp;
the world every couple years is a draining gig,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:41.200
and Downey's superhero commitments kept him&nbsp;
from being able to take on the detective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:46.240
role for a third time. Now that Downey has&nbsp;
finally exited the MCU for good, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:50.880
he finally has the time to team up with&nbsp;
Jude Law's Watson for one more case.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:54.880
The third Sherlock Holmes film will be&nbsp;
helmed by Rocketman director Dexter Fletcher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.360
a departure from the first two films, which were&nbsp;
both directed by Guy Ritchie. Meanwhile, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:04.240
script comes from Narcos creator Chris Brancato.&nbsp;
While Sherlock Holmes 3 was originally scheduled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:09.440
to release on Christmas Day, 2020, it's since&nbsp;
been delayed due to the uncertainty caused by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:15.040
COVID-19 pandemic. After having its theatrical&nbsp;
release bumped from 2020 to December 21,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:20.720
2021, Fletcher remarked in the fall of 2020 that&nbsp;
the sequel is sitting in limbo until things get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:24.880
back on track. While the film obviously&nbsp;
won't make its Christmas 2021 release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:29.520
at the moment, it's suspected that Sherlock&nbsp;
Holmes 3 will hit theaters sometime in 2022.

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:35.600
Disney's live-action reimaginings of their&nbsp;
animated classics have proven to be a home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:40.240
run at the box office, and the live-action&nbsp;
Aladdin was no exception, bringing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:45.840
over $1 billion globally. So it comes as&nbsp;
no surprise that it's getting a follow-up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:51.200
although this one likely won't be modeled directly&nbsp;
off the animated version of the animated sequel.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.880
Few details are known about the Aladdin&nbsp;
sequel, although stars Will Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:59.600
Mena Massoud, and Naomi Scott are all expected&nbsp;
to reprise their respective roles as the Genie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:03.920
Aladdin, and Jasmine. Guy Ritchie is also&nbsp;
expected to return to the director's chair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:08.080
working off a script from John Gatins&nbsp;
and Andrea Berloff. As for the plot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:12.880
it's still very much an unknown, although it's&nbsp;
possible that the sequel could take the form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:18.560
of an adaptation of another folk tale from One&nbsp;
Thousand and One Nights. Aside from that, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.200
everyone's still very much&nbsp;
in the dark on this one.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:28.080
Before Bad Boys for Life had even hit theaters in&nbsp;
early 2020, Sony was already prepping the fourth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:33.840
installment in the Bad Boys franchise. Bad Boys&nbsp;
4 was announced in January 2020 as a follow-up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:39.600
the first three films in the hit buddy cop action&nbsp;
franchise, which first kicked off in 1995 with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:45.440
original Bad Boys. Starring Will Smith and Martin&nbsp;
Lawrence, that original movie follows two Miami&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:50.080
detectives as they investigate a case of stolen&nbsp;
heroin while protecting the witness to a murder.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:55.040
Bad Boys was successful enough to earn&nbsp;
a sequel, which was released in 2003.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.040 --> 00:11:00.000
The third movie, Bad Boys for Life, catches&nbsp;
up with Detectives Lowrey and Burnett&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.360
17 years later, as they investigate a string&nbsp;
of murders with connections to Lowrey's past.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:15.040
"Bad boys bad boys, whatcha gonna do, whatcha&nbsp;
gonna do when we-" "Hey, hey, ah ah, no. Never."

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:19.920
No plot details have yet been revealed about the&nbsp;
fourth film, but the script is being penned by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:24.160
Chris Bremner, who also worked on Bad Boys&nbsp;
for Life. While nothing is official yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:28.080
it's also safe to assume that Smith and&nbsp;
Lawrence will both return for part four.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:31.360
Here's hoping it doesn't take&nbsp;
another 17 years to release.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:37.360
Despite having a pretty definitive ending,&nbsp;
the Oscar nominated Queen flick Bohemian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:43.120
Rhapsody may be getting a sequel. The first film&nbsp;
portrays the early days of the iconic group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:47.600
from its unsteady beginnings in 1970&nbsp;
when Farrokh Bulsara first joined,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:52.240
through the next few decades, as Bulsara changes&nbsp;
his name to Freddie Mercury, rises to fame, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:57.280
eventually splits up the group in the early '80s.&nbsp;
Bohemian Rhapsody ends with the band reuniting for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:03.760
Queen's performance at Live Aid in 1985, before&nbsp;
explaining how Mercury died of AIDS in 1991.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:08.800
There's no word yet on what the plot of Bohemian&nbsp;
Rhapsody 2 could be, whether it would delve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:13.120
into the last six years of Mercury's life, or&nbsp;
whether it would follow the other members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:19.520
the band after his death. In a post on Instagram&nbsp;
Live in 2021, Queen guitarist Brian May said:

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:23.920
"It's going to be hard to follow [Bohemian&nbsp;
Rhapsody] as none of us could have predicted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:28.800
how massive that was going to be. [...] But&nbsp;
yes, we are thinking maybe it could happen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:33.600
but it would have to be a great script. It's&nbsp;
going to take a while to figure that out."

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:37.280
But as far as whether the band has&nbsp;
interest in a sequel, May said:

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:40.960
"We are looking at it. Yeah,&nbsp;
we have been looking at ideas."

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:46.640
While 2021's Cruella was set up to serve&nbsp;
as a prequel to Disney's animated film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:50.720
One Hundred and One Dalmatians, by the time&nbsp;
the end credits rolled, it was clear that there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:55.920
is plenty more of Cruella's story to tell.&nbsp;
Sure enough, Cruella 2 is now in the works,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.920 --> 00:13:01.440
which will see Emma Stone returning to the&nbsp;
role of Estella and her ruthless alter ego,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:06.320
Cruella de Vil. Also coming back is director&nbsp;
Craig Gillespie and writer Tony McNamara,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:10.800
although none of Stone's fellow Cruella cast&nbsp;
members are yet confirmed for the sequel.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:16.720
The first film saw aspiring fashion designer and&nbsp;
petty criminal Estella scheming her way to the top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:22.080
of the fashion industry and usurping the reign&nbsp;
of reigning fashion queen Baroness von Hellman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:27.600
By the end of the film, Cruella has claimed the&nbsp;
Baroness' empire as her own and fully embraced her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:34.160
dark and semi-villainous persona. Yet she still&nbsp;
has a great love of dogs, particularly Dalmatians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:40.080
which begs the question of just how she transforms&nbsp;
into the kind of person who wants to skin them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:45.600
for her coats. Perhaps we'll find out when&nbsp;
Cruella 2 eventually struts into theaters.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:50.720
Producer and director Phil Lord has said&nbsp;
that the team behind the Jump Street movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:55.760
is putting a pin in 23 Jump Street, which&nbsp;
would mark the third outing for Channing Tatum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.760 --> 00:14:00.720
and Jonah Hill. However, the studio is moving&nbsp;
forward with a spinoff of the comedy franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:04.080
this time focusing on a female crime-fighting duo.

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:08.240
The first two Jump Street films follow&nbsp;
a pair of male cops who go undercover at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:12.000
educational institutions in order to&nbsp;
ferret out elusive drug suppliers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:16.720
Presumably, the plot of Jump Street: Now For&nbsp;
Her Pleasure would be much in the same vein.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:21.520
It will also probably exist in the same universe&nbsp;
as the existing Jump Street films, functioning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:27.040
as a continuation of the story started by officers&nbsp;
Morton Schmidt and Greg Jenko in the first movies.

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:31.680
This time, the stars taking the fight to the&nbsp;
streets will be Tiffany Haddish and Zendaya, who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:36.240
will most likely be playing undercover narcotics&nbsp;
officers, similar to Tatum and Hill's characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:40.480
in the first two movies. After directing the first&nbsp;
two Jump Street films, Chris Miller and Phil Lord&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:45.040
will be stepping aside for this third outing,&nbsp;
with Rodney Rothman taking the director's chair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:49.520
Rothman will also be collaborating on the script&nbsp;
with Bob's Burgers writers Lizzie and Wendy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:54.560
Molyneux. Rothman previously helped write the&nbsp;
screenplay for 22 Jump Street, and co-directed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:59.200
Lord and Miller's acclaimed animated film&nbsp;
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse. Sadly, there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:04.560
been no word yet on what the plot will entail — or&nbsp;
whether Schmidt or Jenko might make an appearance.

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:11.040
Sylvester Stallone and The Expendables 4 have&nbsp;
been engaging in a will-they-won't-they dance for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:17.120
a few years now, but it's finally official: The&nbsp;
muscle-bound gang is getting back together again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:20.800
with Scott Waugh directing and&nbsp;
Spenser Cohen writing the script.

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:25.360
In addition to Stallone, the Expendables&nbsp;
franchise has been a veritable who's who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:30.720
of current and former action superstars,&nbsp;
featuring everyone from Mel Gibson to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:36.560
Bruce Willis to Jean-Claude Van Damme to&nbsp;
Chuck Norris and many, many, many more.

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:40.160
"I'm back!"

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:44.480
This time around, we know that Stallone&nbsp;
and Jason Statham are coming back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:49.360
as are Dolph Lundgren and UFC legend&nbsp;
Randy Couture. A number of other stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:55.280
including Megan Fox and 50 Cent, have also&nbsp;
signed onto the film in undisclosed roles. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.280 --> 00:16:00.640
the former holder of the World's Strongest Man&nbsp;
title, Eddie Hall, has personally been offered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:06.000
a role by Stallone himself. Hall will play a&nbsp;
villain, as will martial arts star Iko Uwais,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:09.360
who will apparently be facing off&nbsp;
against Statham's character in the film.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:13.680
Of course, these are still early days for&nbsp;
the project, so don't be surprised to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:17.920
more Expendables veterans return…&nbsp;
and a few other fresh faces, too.

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:23.840
After the massive commercial success of Disney's&nbsp;
photo-realistic remake of The Lion King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:27.440
it seemed like only a matter of time&nbsp;
until a sequel was announced. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:31.920
the director taking the directorial reins&nbsp;
from Jon Favreau for The Lion King 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:37.280
is probably not a name most people would&nbsp;
have expected to hear: Barry Jenkins. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:41.760
Academy Award-winning writer and director is&nbsp;
best known for creating critically-acclaimed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:46.640
dramas with strong racial themes, including&nbsp;
Moonlight and If Beale Street Could Talk.

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:51.360
Jenkins won't be writing The Lion King 2, but&nbsp;
he'll be working from a script by Jeff Nathanson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:56.240
who also penned the first Lion King. While no&nbsp;
specific details of the plot have been revealed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.240 --> 00:17:00.640
we know that it will act as a prequel to&nbsp;
the first film, following Mufasa and Scar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:04.560
in their younger years. It will also&nbsp;
introduce a number of new characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:09.040
though who they are and what animals&nbsp;
they might be has yet to be confirmed.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:12.880
Although The Lion King 2 seems like&nbsp;
an outlier in Jenkins' filmography,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:16.640
the director sounds excited about&nbsp;
working on the sequel for Disney, saying:

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:22.400
"Having the opportunity to work with Disney on&nbsp;
expanding this magnificent tale of friendship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:26.560
love and legacy while furthering&nbsp;
my work chronicling the lives and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:30.480
souls of folk within the African&nbsp;
diaspora is a dream come true."

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:37.280
Some films get theatrical or streaming sequels&nbsp;
while others get turned into TV series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:43.360
but if you're the Nicolas Cage series National&nbsp;
Treasure, you get both. The long-awaited threequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:49.920
to 2004's National Treasure and 2007's National&nbsp;
Treasure: Book of Secrets seems to finally be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:54.800
moving forward at Disney, tapping Bad Boys&nbsp;
4 scribe Chris Bremner to write the script.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.800 --> 00:18:00.240
But that's not all; National Treasure will&nbsp;
also find new life as a Disney+ TV series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:04.320
which producer Jerry Bruckheimer says&nbsp;
is currently in the development process.

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:09.040
While National Treasure 3 is expected to reunite&nbsp;
the cast from the first two films, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:14.160
Cage himself, the TV series will follow a young&nbsp;
woman named Jesse, who embarks on an adventure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:19.120
to uncover a lost Pan-American treasure. Serving&nbsp;
as one of the executive producers for the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:24.000
is Jon Turteltaub, who helmed both of the first&nbsp;
two films and is expected to direct the third.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:28.880
Although the Disney+ series is currently further&nbsp;
along in the development pipeline, with production&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:34.400
set to start in early 2022, Bruckheimer says he's&nbsp;
hopeful that both projects will ultimately come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:39.760
to fruition, delivering a veritable treasure&nbsp;
trove of new National Treasure adventures.

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:46.000
With the open-ended conclusion of the 2020&nbsp;
Charlize Theron action hit The Old Guard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:51.600
it seemed as though the film was begging for a&nbsp;
sequel. Sure enough, The Old Guard 2 is in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:57.600
works for Netflix. The sequel will bring back&nbsp;
star Charlize Theron as Andy, the millennia-old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:02.640
mercenary who, in the first film, realized&nbsp;
her immortality was finally beginning to wane.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:08.000
Also returning will be Marwan Kenzari and Luca&nbsp;
Marinelli, who played Joe and Nicky, respectively,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.680
the life partners for centuries who&nbsp;
also act as part of Andy's group.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:16.800
Production is set to start in the first quarter&nbsp;
of 2022, with Victoria Mahoney attached to direct,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.680
and while no plot details have been released yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:23.200
the first film set up some&nbsp;
intriguing possibilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:28.160
After betraying the other members of their group&nbsp;
and being punished with a century of exile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:34.160
the devious Booker comes face to face with Quynh&nbsp;
, played by Veronica Ngo. Quynh is a former member&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:39.200
of their immortal squad who they had thought&nbsp;
was lost forever at the bottom of the ocean.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:45.280
"I feel her pain, her rage. She feels crazy."

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:49.120
Although Quynh used to be Andy's closest ally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:56.160
centuries of drowning over and over might just&nbsp;
have changed her tune. This intriguing story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:56.160 --> 00:20:01.040
thread will hopefully be followed up when The&nbsp;
Old Guard 2 hits Netflix sometime in the future.

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:08.080
Mere days after the 2021 Chris Pratt sci-fi action&nbsp;
film The Tomorrow War dropped on Amazon Prime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:11.600
Amazon Studios and Skydance were&nbsp;
already talking about a sequel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:15.120
The first film centers around Pratt's&nbsp;
character, who's recruited as a soldier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:20.000
to travel to the future and fight a war to save&nbsp;
humanity. The sequel would reportedly bring back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:25.120
Pratt and the first movie's main cast, along&nbsp;
with director Chris McKay and writer Zach Dean.

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:29.520
The Tomorrow War earned an enthusiastic&nbsp;
reaction from Amazon Prime subscribers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:33.920
who viewed it enough for it to debut as the&nbsp;
number one film across streaming platforms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:38.080
over the July 4th holiday weekend. So&nbsp;
it's no wonder that the studios would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:43.200
be eagerly circling a sequel — although&nbsp;
no specific plans are confirmed yet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:48.240
And while we don't yet know what the story&nbsp;
of a potential The Tomorrow War 2 would be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:52.480
it will hopefully be just as thrilling&nbsp;
and action-packed as the first film.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:57.360
The long-running Insidious franchise&nbsp;
is getting a fifth installment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:57.360 --> 00:21:02.480
and this time, franchise star Patrick Wilson&nbsp;
will be settling into the director's chair.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:06.880
The first two films follow a couple whose&nbsp;
young son is haunted by otherworldly beings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:10.720
while the third and fourth are prequels&nbsp;
that focus on the psychic who aided the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:15.520
heroes of the first two films. Insidious 5&nbsp;
will follow the son from the original movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:19.120
now a decade older, as he heads&nbsp;
off to college. In a statement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:23.040
regarding his directorial duties&nbsp;
on the fifth movie, Wilson said:

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:27.040
"I'm honored and thrilled to be at the&nbsp;
helm of the next Insidious installment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:32.480
which will provide an amazing chance to unpack&nbsp;
everything the Lamberts went through a decade ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:37.360
as well as deal with the consequences of their&nbsp;
choices. [...] Into the further we go..."

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:42.560
"The further" that Wilson is referring to is&nbsp;
the demonic realm that houses the entities which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:47.840
haunt the characters in the Insidious films. The&nbsp;
script for Insidious 5 was penned by Scott Teems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:52.320
and based on a story by Leigh Wannell, who&nbsp;
wrote the first four films in the franchise.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:57.360
Although the original Tron wasn't much&nbsp;
of a hit when it was released in 1982,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:57.360 --> 00:22:02.160
the movie developed a growing cult following in&nbsp;
the decades that followed, which ultimately proved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:06.800
big enough to warrant a sequel. Tron: Legacy&nbsp;
premiered in 2010, starring Garrett Hedlund,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:11.440
Olivia Wilde, and original Tron star Jeff&nbsp;
Bridges. Tron: Legacy did well enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:15.360
earn a sequel of its own, and It Runs in&nbsp;
the Family writer Jesse Wigutow was brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:19.920
aboard in 2012 to pen the script. However,&nbsp;
Disney reportedly couldn't figure out how to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:24.480
best approach a new installment in the Tron&nbsp;
series, and so the project was put on hold.

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:28.960
Now, the third Tron film now appears to be&nbsp;
moving forward again, with Lion director Garth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:33.840
Davis coming aboard to direct and Jared Leto&nbsp;
attached to star. While Davis is not known for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:39.280
the type of big-budget, CGI-heavy filmmaking that&nbsp;
a Tron film would require, insiders say that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:39.280 --> 00:22:43.680
fought hard for the job, eventually convincing&nbsp;
Disney executives that he was the right person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:43.680 --> 00:22:48.560
to bring the Grid back to life. As for Leto, he&nbsp;
may have inadvertently revealed the title for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:48.560 --> 00:22:54.240
the third Tron in a now-deleted tweet confirming&nbsp;
his casting, referring to the film as Tron: Ares.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:54.240 --> 00:22:58.800
Although the project has yet to receive a&nbsp;
green light, Davis' and Leto's involvement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:58.800 --> 00:23:02.760
may signal a light at the end of the&nbsp;
tunnel for this long-gestating threequel.

